<article class="env-definition" id="0C6Z">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0C6Z">Definition <span data-tag="0C6Z">55.3.1</span>.</a> A <em>numerical type</em> $T$ is given by </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  n, m_ i, a_{ij}, w_ i, g_ i  \]
</div>
  <p> where $n \geq 1$ is an integer and $m_ i$, $a_{ij}$, $w_ i$, $g_ i$ are integers for $1 \leq i, j \leq n$ subject to the following conditions </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$m_ i > 0$, $w_ i > 0$, $g_ i \geq 0$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the matrix $A = (a_{ij})$ is symmetric and $a_{ij} \geq 0$ for $i \not= j$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
there is no proper nonempty subset $I \subset \{ 1, \ldots , n\} $ such that $a_{ij} = 0$ for $i \in I$, $j \not\in I$, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
for each $i$ we have $\sum _ j a_{ij}m_ j = 0$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$w_ i | a_{ij}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>